Inflation without repeated I/O; measure cache off by default; lost in-layout requests; SurfaceView keeps frames

Measured with MACAPK_LAYOUT_SAMPLER=1 (new: the draw sampler over the measure+layout pass, with app-frame, wait-site and callee reports) on Instagram's tab switches (first layouts of 100-450 ms):
- TypedArray.getFont re-read and re-parsed the font file for every TextView with a fontFamily: 29% of those layouts. Resources caches Typefaces by font resource (and weight/italic).
- File-backed ColorStateLists were re-read out of the APK and re-parsed for every TextView: Resources caches them by (id, theme style stack), cleared on a configuration change.
- LayoutInflater.tryCtor looked constructors up by reflection (a thrown NoSuchMethodException per miss) on every inflated view; FrameLayout.findLpField did the same per child per layout. Both cached.
- buildLP / merge / include log lines on every inflated element now need MACAPK_TRACE_INFLATE=1.
After these the sampled layout time is the app's own RecyclerView/Coordinator/Compose work.

MACAPK_MEASURE_CACHE (0045) is now OFF by default: with it Instagram's music sheet kept a mid-animation 6-170 px content area in 10 of 12 openings; without it 12 of 12 were right. The lost re-measure was not found. Kept: requestLayout during the layout pass is recorded and re-issued up the whole chain afterwards (AOSP requestLayoutDuringLayout), and setMinimumHeight/Width request layout (AOSP).

FRAMESPEED S1: no frame is skipped for empty damage while a SurfaceView is shown (its buffer-fed layer is sized and pulled at present time). MACAPK_DAMAGE_VALIDATE also checks the skip (claims one pixel instead); the off-window skip rule was dropped after the validator caught a visible caption it skipped.

